Third-party components

- **chibicc**, Rui Ueyama, MIT. Source: https://github.com/rui314/chibicc,
  revision `90d1f7f199cc55b13c7fdb5839d1409806633fdb`.
  License: `user/chibicc/LICENSE`. This is an altered KalyOS port: native tool
  paths, static linking and assembly output adapted for kaly-as.
- **xcc**, tyfkda, MIT. Source: https://github.com/tyfkda/xcc,
  revision `9eea241c1331d54730b9173cfb11c4dea7c893a4`.
  License: `user/xcc/LICENSE`. This is an altered KalyOS port of its assembler,
  linker and utilities: comments, two-operand IMUL, ELF mapping/relocations,
  object detection and subsection collection. The SDK `ar.h` and `elf.h`
  derive from this MIT distribution; the same license applies to those copies.
- **TinyGL**, Fabrice Bellard, Gek (DMHSW), C-Chads, permissive zlib-style license.
  Source: https://github.com/C-Chads/tinygl,
  revision `36a7987e7bebfda19615ea33341b1cc0ff9c3b13`.
  License: `user/kalygl/vendor/tinygl/LICENSE`. KalyGL acknowledges the original
  renderer and authors. This is an altered source distribution, not upstream:
  features enable error checking and polygons; readback, depth clearing,
  viewport bounds and query errors are adapted; renderer/version strings
  identify KalyGL. Context/presentation adaptation is in `user/kalygl/src`.
  The unused SDL examples were removed from the working tree and are not built
  or linked. No SDL dependency is introduced.

Original license files and copyright notices are preserved. TinyCC is not a
project dependency and is not included in this distribution.

The vendored working trees are reduced to the C sources and headers required
by the KalyOS build plus compiler builtin headers and original license notices.
Vendor Git histories, frontend/libc components of xcc, other architectures,
demos, documentation, tests and unused build tooling are not distributed.
Only the root KalyOS Git repository is retained. user/libc is the sole libc
implementation; its same PIC objects produce libc.a and libc.so.
